{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-351421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=6t+2.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=2.$\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=2.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(6t+2)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =(3{t}^{2}+2t){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[3(2)^{2}+2(2)]-[3(1)^{2}+2(1)] \\\\  & =[12+4]-[3+2] \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15"} {"question" "q-351421" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351421" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t-1}.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=5.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=5.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}(\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t-1})\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =(t-1)^{3/2}\\,{|}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =(5-1)^{3/2}-(1-1)^{3/2} \\\\  & =8-0 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15"} {"question" "q-351431" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351431" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-19494" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)={t}^{2}-7t+10.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=2$ and $t=5?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-19494" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}({t}^{2}-7t+10)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{7}{2}{t}^{2}+10t)|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}(5)^{3}-\\frac{7}{2}(5)^{2}+10(5)]-[\\frac{1}{3}(2)^{3}-\\frac{7}{2}(2)^{2}+10(2)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{125}{3}-\\frac{175}{2}+50]-[\\frac{8}{3}-14+20] \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{6}-\\frac{26}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo the total displacement between $t=2$ and $t=5$ is $-\\frac{9}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-19494" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15"} {"question" "q-19494" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-19494" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{25}{6}"] ["math" "-\\frac{26}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{9}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{25}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{27}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-19494" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{9}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=16-9{t}^{2}.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=3$ and $t=4.$\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=3$ and $t=4.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(16-9{t}^{2})\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & ={(16t-3{t}^{3})|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =[16(4)-3(4)^{3}]-[16(3)-3(3)^{3}] \\\\  & =[64-192]-[48-81] \\\\  & =-95.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15"} {"question" "q-351430" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351430" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-95"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-120986" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=6{t}^{2}+t-\\frac{3}{2}.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=4?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-120986" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(6{t}^{2}+t-\\frac{3}{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(2{t}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}t)|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =[2(4)^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}(4)^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}(4)]-[2(1)^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}(1)] \\\\  & =[128+8-6]-[2+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}] \\\\  & =130-1 \\\\  & =129.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=4$ is $129.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-120986" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15"} {"question" "q-120986" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-120986" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "127"] ["math" "128"] ["math" "129"] ["math" "130"] ["math" "131"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-120986" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "129"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ At time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ the particle is located at the position $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=\\pi ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is equal to its position at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\pi ].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\pi )=x(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{2}+{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3})]}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+([-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3})]-[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-(-\\frac{1}{2})+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-121007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=3.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{6}].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =\\frac{7}{2}+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3+{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =3+([\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]-[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]) \\\\  & =3+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =3+(0-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =3+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is $x=\\frac{7}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-81506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t)=3{e}^{3t-1}.$ At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=2{e}^{2}.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=5?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=5$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,5].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(5)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(5) & =2{e}^{2}+{\\int }_{1}^{5}3{e}^{3t-1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}+{[{e}^{3t-1}]}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}+({e}^{3(5)-1}-{e}^{3(1)-1}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}+({e}^{14}-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}+{e}^{14}-{e}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2}+{e}^{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=5$ is $x={e}^{2}+{e}^{14}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{e}^{2}+{e}^{14}"] ["math" "{e}^{14}-{e}^{2}+1"] ["math" "{e}^{16}-{e}^{2}+1"] ["math" "{e}^{2}+{e}^{14}"] ["math" "{e}^{2}+{e}^{16}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-121000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{2}+{e}^{14}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-120998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t)={e}^{2t+1}.$ At time $t=0.5$ the particle is located at the position $x={e}^{2}.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-120998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=2$ is equal to its position at $t=0.5$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0.5,2].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(2)=x(0.5)+{\\int }_{0.5}^{2}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) & ={e}^{2}+{\\int }_{0.5}^{2}{e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={e}^{2}+{[\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t+1}]}_{0.5}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2}+(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2(2)+1}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2(0.5)+1}) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}+(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{5}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}+{e}^{5}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=2$ is $x=\\frac{{e}^{2}+{e}^{5}}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-120998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15"} {"question" "q-120998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-120998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2}+{e}^{5}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{5}}{2}"] ["math" "{e}^{2}+{e}^{5}"] ["math" "{e}^{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-120998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{2}+{e}^{5}}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351444" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(t)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t).$ At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=3.$ \nFind the position of the particle at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351444" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{3}].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =3+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(t)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3+{[\\operatorname{sec}⁡(t)]}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =3+\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0) \\\\  & =3+2-1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ is $x=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351444" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15"} {"question" "q-351444" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351444" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/4c50effa85cc82dfc22a65f3792780a99b2876b77de173993b43dead23b0c1d7.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0,$ the particle is located at the position $x=-4.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=6?$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=6$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=6$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,6].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(6)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(0)=-4$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=0$ to $t=6.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(6)=-4+10=6.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=6$ is $x=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15"} {"question" "q-351479" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351479" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-348321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/e51b807bc238b140215a8a753fcfe778b14735e723dd5cb43b8aab22039a8e8e.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0,$ the particle is located at the position $x=-2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-348321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,4].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(0)=-2$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=0$ to $t=4.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=12.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(4)=-2+12=10.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-348321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15"} {"question" "q-348321" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-348321" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/005c8cf386537414fb0504fa26095f54fbeeaa0f88941bef41fffaf75f791ed3.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2,$ the particle is located at the position $x=8.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=7?$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=7$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,7].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(7)=x(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=8$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{2}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=7.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(7)=8+(-3)=5.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15"} {"question" "q-351502" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351502" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake