5"} {"question" "q-81509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-81509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-81509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/4245a22d62605e68022fc2f02358f8f900e5370a02c04c973d0ea359249f62b6.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0,$ the particle is located at the position $x=4.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,4].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(0)=4$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=0$ to $t=4.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(4)=4+(-1)=3.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3d8e7114095d71cce841251be3bbf2c294a0f3065aaac393ba0dc20190486e15"} {"question" "q-351500" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "q-351500" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c80424406a4518c6f6e53cfdc447c2b85a9e49cf5459fa1456f2110a19df34e"} {"question" "e-568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t) = 2t + 3t^2.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=3?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-568.json" "file_sha256" "902c39eabe7fa5fcd71f6ab8a5ed2992b55ce2683462c85bb8214aade1abfe5e"} {"question" "e-568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(2t+3{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={({t}^{2}+{t}^{3})|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =[{3}^{2}+{3}^{3}]-[{1}^{2}+{1}^{3}] \\\\  & =[9+27]-[1+1] \\\\  & =36-2 \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=3$ is $34.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-568.json" "file_sha256" "902c39eabe7fa5fcd71f6ab8a5ed2992b55ce2683462c85bb8214aade1abfe5e"} {"question" "e-7128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t) = 6t^2 +4t.$ At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-20.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-7128.json" "file_sha256" "cf39f066a9bebfa423e36e53e5d26410735ad5e78e6a00d4cf8f063443a3f4c3"} {"question" "e-7128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in[2,4].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4) = x(2) + \\int_2^4 v(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(4) & =-20+{\\int }_{2}^{4}(6{t}^{2}+4t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =-20+{[2{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =-20+([2(4)^{3}+2(4)^{2}]-[2(2)^{3}+2(2)^{2}]) \\\\  & =-20+([128+32]-[16+8]) \\\\  & =-20+(160-24) \\\\  & =-20+136 \\\\  & =116.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=116.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-7128.json" "file_sha256" "cf39f066a9bebfa423e36e53e5d26410735ad5e78e6a00d4cf8f063443a3f4c3"} {"question" "e-7129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/900988cb8ec54abcafc256a34c685829d2f5f00cdca373ad84dfa0ef70cc3957.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-1.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=8?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-7129.json" "file_sha256" "d2c6d2782d678e247239b6b0463883ecc5c6091a11425d6c62613dbf202fecf5"} {"question" "e-7129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position of the particle at $t = 8$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,8].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(8) = x(2)+ \\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm d t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=-1$, and we can compute the integral $\\displaystyle\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=8.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt = 6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(8) = -1+ 6 = 5\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=8$ is $x=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/example-7129.json" "file_sha256" "d2c6d2782d678e247239b6b0463883ecc5c6091a11425d6c62613dbf202fecf5"}] "usage" {"e-568" [] "e-7128" [] "e-7129" []} "basis" 1189 "retractions" [[17592186175707 :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t) = 2t + 3t^2$. What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=3$?"] [17592186175707 :question/worked-solution "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd &= ∫_{1}^{3}(2t + 3t^{2})dt \\\\\n&= (t^{2} + t^{3}) \\mid _{1}^{3} \\\\\n&= [3^{2} + 3^{3}] - [1^{2} + 1^{3}] \\\\\n&= [9 + 27] - [1 + 1] \\\\\n&= 36 - 2 \\\\\n&= 34\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=3$ is $34$."] [17592186175719 :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t) = 6t^2 +4t$. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-20$. What is the position of the particle at time $t=4$?"] [17592186175719 :question/worked-solution "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in[2,4]$. Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4) = x(2) + \\int_2^4 v(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx(4) &= -20 + ∫_{2}^{4}(6t^{2} + 4t)dt \\\\\n&=-20 + [2t^{3} + 2t^{2}]_{2}^{4} \\\\\n&=-20 + ([2(4)^{3} + 2(4)^{2}] - [2(2)^{3} + 2(2)^{2}]) \\\\\n&=-20 + ([128 + 32] - [16 + 8]) \\\\\n&=-20 + (160 - 24) \\\\\n&=-20 + 136 \\\\\n&= 116\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=116$."] [17592186175720 :question/problem "The graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-1$. What is the position of the particle at time $t=8$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3576/Source/Images/1e5634171531dd04f9da7173af00e15c.png)"] [17592186175720 :question/worked-solution "The position of the particle at $t = 8$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,8]$. Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(8) = x(2)+ \\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm d t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=-1$, and we can compute the integral $\\displaystyle\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=8$. Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt = 6\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(8) = -1+ 6 = 5\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=8$ is $x=5$."]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
